---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.png";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A proof tree drawn as flat black boxes joined by thin lines on warm cream, each box holding a short Metamath statement, branching upward from one root"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Learn to read a Metamath database, prove theorems in it, and write a program
    that checks the proofs. Each week has a Monday lecture and a Wednesday lab.
    The first two labs install the tools and read small databases; from week 3
    every lab ends with a theorem to prove in mmj2, and a proof counts when the
    verifier accepts it. From week 5 you are also writing your own verifier, in a
    language of your choice, marked against a test suite the course provides.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who wants to learn Metamath. You need to have programmed before, in
    any language, because the verifier project is a program. You do not need to
    have studied logic: the language is taught from nothing in the first three
    weeks, and every symbol is explained when it first appears. If you have met
    formal logic already, the first three weeks will be quick and the rest will
    not.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title="Lectures" href="/lectures/">
      <p>What each of the twelve weeks covers, and the reading behind it.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>What to bring to each lab, what happens in it, and what leaves the room.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>Lab proofs, the definition exercise and the verifier project: what each is worth and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and who to ask about what.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
